From Local Docker Applications to Cloud-Native MCP Services

Building an AI-Ready Architecture with Docker, Kubernetes, and the Model Context Protocol (MCP)

Abstract

As AI agents become first-class software consumers, traditional APIs are evolving into discoverable, tool-enabled services. The Model Context Protocol (MCP) provides a standardized mechanism for exposing capabilities to AI systems.

This guide demonstrates how to transform an existing local Dockerized application into a cloud-native MCP-enabled service deployable on Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, or Kubernetes platforms.


